# Immutable state identity profile v5

The full Pyparsing stage trace reaches repeated `RepositoryState.state_cid`
serialization during native source binding. A state contains 3,957 symbols and
55,859 edges. The native property serializes every record on every access;
`_state_cid_of` accesses the property for both `hasattr` and retrieval. No source
bytes change during this immutable-state operation.

The isolated profile adds one private, nonconstructor, noncomparing field to
`RepositoryState`. It memoizes the canonical CID only for the exact native state
class containing exact native symbol, artifact, edge and span records. These
constructors copy structured input into recursive mapping proxies/tuples and
freeze their fields. Subclasses retain the original uncached property behavior.
Every access still checks the exact record types, and replacing the codec
function invalidates the process-local memo. The cache is absent from all durable
schemas and identity payloads. A new state or `dataclasses.replace` starts empty;
restoration still independently computes identity and rejects a claimed mismatch.

This assumes the existing closed native value-object discipline: source and codec
configuration remain frozen, and no code bypasses dataclass immutability through
reflection or `object.__setattr__`. It is not a defense against arbitrary code
execution in the native interpreter. The runtime source inventory is checked by
the context service before and after its operations. The previous profile remains
unchanged. This is explicitly a different measured implementation profile.

Native source retrieval is unchanged. It binds the caller's expected state CID,
resolves the actual symbol, retrieves source twice, recomputes its content CID,
checks the reads agree, and verifies source spans. No source bytes, execution
results, proof results, or admission decisions are cached. Changed source requires
new source capture, scan, state, bundle and context pack.

Qualification is recorded separately in `state_identity_validation_v5/`: fresh
processes using the parent and new profiles compare complete XML states, serialized
identities, semantic roots and all reachable block bytes for unchanged source and
an authored comment change with cold and incremental scanning. Additional controls
check detached serialization, frozen fields, changed-state reconstruction,
tampered restore, dynamic subclass behavior, and repeated native materialization
with corrupt source rejection. `state_identity_native_regression_v5/` runs the
159 existing content, state, source, freshness, model, scanner, identity and
snapshot authority tests. `results_v12_full_state_identity/` is a distinct full
XML/Pyparsing producer/consumer run under the existing 600-second process bound.
None of these operations sends provider requests or establishes token savings.
